Package: secureshellgo
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libsecret-1-0, libgtk-3-0
# libsecret-1-0 is only the *client* of the Secret Service API — it needs a
# daemon on the other end of D-Bus to actually store anything. Without one,
# saving a password fails with "no system keyring is available", which reads
# to the user as a broken app rather than a missing component.
#
# gnome-keyring is listed first because it is what actually ships
# /usr/share/dbus-1/services/org.freedesktop.secrets.service on Ubuntu, and
# apt satisfies an alternation with the first available option — so a plain
# desktop install gets a working provider without being asked. The rest are
# there so a machine that already runs one of them is not made to pull GNOME
# bits in as well: on KDE the daemon is kwalletd, not the kwalletmanager GUI,
# which only administers wallets and registers nothing on D-Bus.
Recommends: gnome-keyring | kwalletd6 | kwalletd5 | keepassxc
Description: SSH terminal and SFTP client with strict host-key verification
 SecureShell Go is a fast, security-first SSH terminal and SFTP client for
 Linux servers. Run a real interactive xterm-256color shell and transfer
 files over SFTP, with trust-on-first-use host-key verification at the
 core.
 .
 A changed host key blocks the connection outright, with SHA256
 fingerprints shown for out-of-band verification and an explicit,
 checkbox-gated override required to proceed. Passwords, private keys, and
 passphrases are kept only in encrypted secure storage.
 .
 Includes a saved host manager, password and private-key authentication,
 and an SFTP file browser for uploads, downloads, and whole-folder
 transfers, alongside the terminal in the same session.
